Assertions:
[NAV] URL is {{FRONT_URL}}/company/my-customers/@td(ORG_ACME.id) {OBSERVED}
[DOM] Customer information and Orders sections are both visible on the profile page {OBSERVED}
[STATE] the rendered organization details match @td(ORG_ACME.name) (the clicked row's org) {OBSERVED}

[DOM] the page heading (h1) displays the organization name @td(ORG_ACME.name) {OBSERVED}
[DOM] the page heading area shows an organization icon (building placeholder acceptable; a null iconUrl is OK, not a failure) {OBSERVED}
[DOM] the Customer information card shows a non-empty account type value (sourced from accountType) {OBSERVED}
[DOM] the Customer information card shows a non-empty phone value {OBSERVED}

Preconditions:
[PRE:CLEAR_SESSION]
[PRE:SIGNIN_AS:SR_REP_PRIMARY]
@td(ORG_ACME.id) has a fully seeded address (line1/city/regionName/postalCode/countryCode) — pairs with 050m SR-GQL-036 (backend contract for this exact field set). DOM-VERIFIED (2026-07-17, theme pr-2383): the shipped profile renders a COMPACT ship-to ("<City>, <Region>" only), not the full address block originally assumed. Backend SR-GQL-036 exposes the FULL address (line1/postalCode/countryCode) — the storefront's own salesRepCustomer query deliberately narrows the field selection to city+region for this card. DESIGN-CONFIRM (VCST-5308): is the compact ship-to intended, or should the profile show the full address?

[PRE:CLEAR_SESSION]
[PRE:SIGNIN_AS:SR_REP_PRIMARY]
@td(ORG_ACME.id) has an explicit Owner contact resolved as primaryContact (mirrors 050m SR-GQL-019). DOM-VERIFIED (2026-07-17, theme pr-2383): the shipped profile renders the primary contact's NAME ONLY — no email, phone, or photo for the contact. The Customer-information card's "Phone" field is salesRepCustomer.phone (org-level, already covered by SR-CP-005), not primaryContact.phone. DESIGN-CONFIRM (VCST-5308): is name-only primary contact intended, or should email/phone/photo also render?

[PRE:CLEAR_SESSION]
[PRE:SIGNIN_AS:SR_REP_PRIMARY]
@td(ORG_ACME.id) has >=2 orders with distinct createdDate (mirrors 050m SR-GQL-022 default sort createdDate:desc).

[PRE:CLEAR_SESSION]
[PRE:SIGNIN_AS:SR_REP_PRIMARY]
@td(ORG_ACME.id) has orders in >=2 distinct statuses (mirrors 050m SR-GQL-033 salesRepOrderFilterRules). RESOLVED live 2026-07-24 (TLC-2026-07-24-1906, build SalesRep pr-4-6596 / theme pr-2395): order-status filtering IS in scope — chips populate from salesRepOrderFilterRules and clicking a chip filters via salesRepOrders(filter:).

[PRE:CLEAR_SESSION]
[PRE:SIGNIN_AS:SR_REP_PRIMARY]
@td(ORG_ACME.id) has at least one order with status Cancelled and a non-zero total. Storefront culture switched to a non-English locale. Pairs with 050m SR-GQL-031 (statusDisplayValue) and SR-GQL-037 (total.formattedAmount, nested MoneyType — CONFIRMED via Phase-5 live introspection 2026-07-17) — this case only bridges the rendered UI to those already-verified API contracts. Fails on pr-2383: profile Orders query selects raw `status`, not `statusDisplayValue` — status badge stays English under /de. Product bug, not a test defect; assertion intentionally left as-is (correctly grounds the desired behavior and catches the real bug).

[PRE:CLEAR_SESSION]
[PRE:SIGNIN_AS:SR_REP_PRIMARY]
@td(ORG_ACME.id) has >=1 order with a known number, createdDate, and itemsCount > 0 (mirrors 050m SR-GQL-022). DOM-VERIFIED (2026-07-17, theme pr-2383): the profile Orders table renders the order number WITHOUT a "#" prefix — omitted here vs the list-page (089 SR-FE-004) and order-details conventions; logged as a cosmetic inconsistency, not a functional defect.

Assertions:
[DOM] each order row shows a non-empty order number (no "#" prefix in this table, unlike 089's list-page convention — see note) {OBSERVED}
[DOM] each order row has a formatted date visible, e.g. "Jul 17, 2026" (no raw ISO timestamp) {OBSERVED}
[DOM] each order row has a non-zero item count visible {OBSERVED}

Preconditions:
[PRE:CLEAR_SESSION]
[PRE:SIGNIN_AS:SR_REP_PRIMARY]
@td(ORG_ACME.id) has >=1 order. Carries over the ordering-asymmetry/403 concern documented at the list-page layer in 089 SR-FE-006 — unresolved there, so unresolved here.

Assertions:
[DOM] a Sales widgets section/container is present on the profile page {OBSERVED}
[STATE] the widgets container renders alongside the Customer information and Orders sections on the same profile page (not on a separate route) {OBSERVED}
[STATE] verify whether the 4 KPI widgets now render values traceable to salesRepCustomerOrderStatistics(organizationId: @td(ORG_ACME.id)) for this org, or still render mock/placeholder values (Ivan Kalachikov's VCST-5485 comment: "the set of implemented widgets is limited by BE data readiness... statistic widgets are built on mock data yet" — that comment targets the Hub Dashboard per VCST-5485, but VCST-5309's own review status suggests the profile widgets may be in the same state) {HYPOTHESIS}

Steps:
[NAV] {{FRONT_URL}}/sign-in
[ACT] fill 'Email': {{email}}
[ACT] fill 'Password': {{password}}
[ACT] click 'Sign in'
[WAIT] sign-in attempt settles

Assertions:
[NETWORK] the sign-in attempt receives HTTP 400 on /connect/token {OBSERVED}
[DOM] the sign-in form surfaces an error indicating access to the organization has been blocked (message observed: "Your access to this organization has been blocked") {OBSERVED}
[STATE] no authenticated session is established — the rep never reaches an authenticated state, so {{locked_org}}'s profile at /company/my-customers/{{locked_org}} is unreachable by construction (no session exists to attempt navigation with) {SPEC}

[DOM] a "Quick actions" widget/section is visible on the profile page alongside Customer information, Orders, and Sales widgets {OBSERVED}
[DOM] the Quick actions widget is visible with exactly 4 tiles arranged in a 2x2 grid {DOC}
[DOM] the "Send email" tile is visible and enabled (not greyed out) {OBSERVED}

[DOM] the communication modal is absent (closed) after a successful send {OBSERVED}
[DOM] a success toast/notification is visible {OBSERVED}
[STATE] the profile page (Customer information / Orders / Sales widgets) remains rendered and interactive after the modal closes {OBSERVED}

[DOM] the customer-communication modal opens with Title, Message, Email and Push fields all visible and not clipped at 768px {OBSERVED}
[DOM] the Cancel and Send buttons are both visible/reachable in the modal footer {OBSERVED}
[DOM] the modal subtitle names @td(ORG_ACME.name) — the profile's own organization {OBSERVED}
[STATE] no horizontal overflow and no content clipped at 768px {OBSERVED}

[DOM] an "MTD" (month-to-date) purchases stat tile is visible showing a non-negative order count {SPEC}
[DOM] the same tile shows an average-order-value (AOV) formatted as currency {SPEC}
[DOM] the same tile shows a total-purchases value formatted as currency {SPEC}

[DOM] a "YTD" (year-to-date) purchases stat tile is visible showing a non-negative order count {SPEC}
[DOM] the same tile shows an AOV formatted as currency {SPEC}
[DOM] the same tile shows a total-purchases value formatted as currency, and the YTD total is >= the MTD total from SR-CP-028 for the same org {SPEC}

[DOM] the MTD or YTD stat tile shows a period-over-period $ change value (formatted currency, signed +/-) {SPEC}
[DOM] the same tile shows a % change value alongside the $ change {SPEC}
[STATE] IF the previous-period total for this org is zero, the % change is rendered as a graceful placeholder (e.g. "—" or "N/A"), NOT NaN/Infinity/a raw null {SPEC}

[DOM] a "Top products purchased" block/section is visible on the profile page {SPEC}
[COUNT] the block shows at most 5 product rows (take default) {SPEC}
[DOM] each row shows a product name, SKU, image (or placeholder), and a units-purchased count, with rows ordered by units descending {SPEC}
